<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Armistice of Mudros</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armistice-of-11-november-1918">Armistice</a> of Mudros, signed on 30 October 1918 aboard HMS <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agamemnon">Agamemnon</a> in Mudros harbour on the island of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lemnos">Lemnos</a>, ended fighting between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>. It opened the Dardanelles, demobilised the Ottoman army and allowed the Allies to occupy strategic points, leading to the occupation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> and other territories.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/armistice-of-mudros.jpg" alt="Armistice of Mudros" width="320" height="196" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agamemnon_at_Mudros.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>The <b>Armistice of Mudros</b> in 1918 and the Treaty of Sèvres of 1920 proposed the empire's partition, and the Allied occupation of Istanbul in 1918 and İzmir in 1919 set off the Turkish National Movement under Mustafa Kemal Pasha.</blockquote><a href="/empire/republic-of-turkey">Republic of Turkey · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the <b>Armistice of Mudros</b>, British and then French forces occupied Cilicia from late 1918, and in 1919 France took over full responsibility, administering it as part of the Occupied Enemy Territory Administration.</blockquote><a href="/state/french-cilicia">French Cilicia</a></li><li><blockquote>Under the <b>Armistice of Mudros</b> in October 1918, the Ottoman Empire had to withdraw from Kars, Ardahan and Batum, lands it had gained by the Treaty of Brest-Litovsk.</blockquote><a href="/state/southwestern-caucasian-republic">Southwestern Caucasian Republic</a></li></ul></section>
